  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\n\nIn the latest open beta \"SetManualAvatarScalingAllowed(true)\" was changed to no longer set a player back to their preference height which is great!  \n\nHowever, there is one problem with that, there is no way to set a player back to their preference height. Which is something worlds might want to do if a player is e.g. outside of an area where the world would like to take control about it.  \n\nIn my AudioShrink world I have something called \"Safe Zones\", in these zones I would for example like to set the player back to their preference height.  \n\n(Preference Height being the height that they chose with the Height Slider)\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nThere are multiple way on how this functionality could be added back:\n\n1. Add a \"SetAvatarEyeHeithToPreferenceHeight\" method, this could be used to well, set the player back to their preference height.\n\n2. Add a GetAvatarPreferenceHeight(VRCPlayerAPI playerApi, float preferenceHeight) method, this could be used to get the players preference height which in return could be used to set the player to it.\n\nAdding either (or even both) would be great! As it would allow us give the player back their original height after we are done with what ever we did with them before though Udon.",
